come.\n\nFor you are our salvation, Lord,\nour refuge and our great reward;\nwithout your grace we waste away\nlike flowers that wither and decay.\n\nTo heal the sick, stretch out thine hand,\nand make the fallen sinner stand;\nshine out, and let your light restore\nearth\'s own true loveliness once more.\n\nTo you, O Christ, all praises be,\nwho comes to set your people free;\nwhom with the Father we adore\nand with the Spirit evermore.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(372,'349','All my heart this night rejoices','Catherine Winkworth 1827-78',NULL,'in this version Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(373,'350','Angels from the realms of glory','James Montgomery 1771-1854, verse 5 from The Christmas Box 1825',NULL,'vv 1-3, 5 in this version Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(374,'351','Child of the stable\'s secret birth','Timothy Dudley-Smith','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(375,'352','Christians, awake! Salute the happy morn','J. Byrom 1692-1763',NULL,'In this version, Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(376,'353','Earth gave him no welcome','Margaret Clarkson',NULL,'1976 Singspiration Music / Brentwood Benson Music Publishing / Copycare','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(377,'354','Earth lies spellbound in darkness','Graham Kendrick','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(378,'355','Behold, the great Creator makes','Thomas Pestel 1584-1659','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His birth and childhood'),(379,'356','Earth was waiting, spent and restless','Wa