is birth and childhood'),(412,'389','Christ our Redeemer knew temptation\'s hour','Timothy Dudley-Smith',NULL,'Author','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(413,'390','Forty days and forty nights','George H Smyttan 1822-70','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(414,'391','How good, Lord, to be here!','J Armitage Robinson 1858-1933','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(415,'392','When Jesus led his chosen three','Christopher Idle','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(416,'393','Transfigured Christ, none comprehends','Alan Gaunt','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(417,'394','He left his home of perfect light','Stephen Crowter','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(418,'395','All praise to Christ, our Lord and King divine','F B Tucker  1895-1984, ALT','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(419,'396','From heaven you came, helpless babe','Graham Kendrick',NULL,'1983 Kingsway\'s Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(420,'397','He walked where I walk','Graham Kendrick','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(421,'398','How humble Moses was, who met','Phil Heaps. ALT','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(422,'399','I have a friend whose faithful love','C A Tydeman','I have a friend whose faithful love\nIs more than all the world to me;\nIt\'s higher that the heights above,\nAnd deeper than the deepest sea;\nSo old, so new, so strong, so true;\nBefore the earth received its frame,\nHe loved me - bless His holy name!\n\nHe held the highest place above,\nAdored by all the sons of flame,\nYet, such His self-denying love,\nHe laid aside His crown and came\nTo seek the lost, and at the cost\nOf heavenly rant and earthly fame,\nHe sought me - bless His holy name!\n\nIt was a lonely path He trod,\nFrom every human soul apart;\nKnown only to Himself and God\nWas all the grief that filled His heart:\nYet from His track He turned not back\nTill where I lay in want and shame\nHe found me - bless His holy name!\n\nThen dawned at last that day of dread\nWhen, desolate but undismayed,\nWith wearied frame and thorn-crowned head\nHe, now forsaken and betrayed,\nWent up for me to Calvary,\nAnd dying there in grief and shame\nHe saved me - bless His holy name!\n\nLong as I live my song shall tell\nThe wonders of His matchless love:\nAnd when at last I rise to dwell\nIn that bright home prepared above,\nMy joy shall be His face to see,\nAnd bowing then with loud acclaim,\nI\'ll praise Him - bless His holy name!\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(423,'400','Lord, you left your throne and your kingly crown','Emily E S Elliott 1836-97','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(424,'401','My dear Redeemer and my Lord','Isaac Watts 1674-1748','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(425,'402','O changeless Christ, for ever new','Timothy Dudley-Smith','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(426,'403','My song is love unknown','Samuel Crossman 1624-83',NULL,'1-4,7 in this version Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(427,'404','That priceless gift what tongue can tell','J Alec Motyer',NULL,'J Alec Motyer','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(428,'405','The darkness turns to dawn','Timothy Dudley-Smith',NULL,'Timothy Dudley-Smith','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(429,'406','We were not there to see you come','John H Gurney 1802-62 and others','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(430,'407','All glory, praise and honour','Theodulph of Orleans c.750-821, trans. John Mason Neale 1818-66',NULL,'Verses 3 and 4 ','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(431,'408','Ride on, ride on in majesty','H. H. Milman 1791-1868',NULL,'in this version Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His life and ministry'),(432,'409','Behold the amazing sight!','Philip Doddridge 1702-51',NULL,'in this version Praise Trust','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(433,'410','A purple robe, a crown of thorn','Tmothy Dudley;Smith','A purple robe, a crown of thorn,\nA reed in his right hand;\nBefore the soldier','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(434,'411','Alas! And did my Saviour bleed','Isaac Watts 1674-1748',NULL,'in this version, Praise Trust','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(435,'412','Ah, holy Jesus, how have you offended','Robert Bridges 1844-1930, ALT. After Johann Heermann 1585','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(436,'413','Approach with awe this holiest place','Timothy Dudley-Smith',NULL,'Author','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(437,'414','At the cross of Jesus','John Eddison',NULL,'Scripture Union','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(438,'415','Come and see, come and see','Graham Kendrick',NULL,'1989 Make Way Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(439,'416','Deep is the love of Jesus','Olive and Noel Allsup','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(440,'417','Give me a sight, O Saviour','Katharine A M Kelly 1869-1942',NULL,'National Young Life Campaign','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(441,'418','Go to dark Gethsemane','James Montgomery 1771-1854','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(442,'419','Hark! The voice of love and mercy','Jonathan Evans 1748-1809','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(443,'420','He stood before the court','Christopher Idle','He stood before the court\non trial instead of us;\nhe met its power to hurt,\ncondemned to face the cross;\nour King, accused\nof treachery;\nour God, abused\nfor blasphemy!\n\nThese are the crimes that tell\nthe tale of human guilt;\nour sins, our death, our hell,\non these the case is built;\nto this world\'s powers\ntheir Lord stays dumb;\nthe guilt is ours,\nno answers come.\n\nThe sentence must be passed,\nthe unknown prisoner killed;\nthe price is paid at last,\nthe law of God fulfilled;\nhe takes our blame,\nand from that day\nthe accuser\'s claim\nis wiped away.\n\nShall we be judged and tried?\nIn Christ our trial is done;\nwe live, for he has died,\nour condemnation gone;\nin Christ are we\nboth dead and raised -\nalive and free-\nhis name be praised!\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(444,'421','Glory be to Jesus','Italian c.1815 Trans. Edward Caswall 1814-78','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(445,'422','He was pierced for our transgressions','Maggi Dawn',NULL,'1987 Kingsway\'s Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(446,'423','Higher than the hills','Norman J Clayton 1903-92',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(447,'424','Here is love, vast as the ocean','William Rees 1802-83 translated William Edwards 1848-1929',NULL,'Executors of Miss Anita Edwards','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(448,'425','His hands were pierced, the hands that made','D Wood','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(449,'426','How deep the Father\'s love for us','Stuart Townend','How deep the Father\'s love for us,\nHow vast beyond all measure,\nThat He should give His only Son\nTo make a wretch His treasure.\nHow great the pain of searing loss -\nThe Father turns His face away,\nAs wounds which mar the Chosen One\nBring many sons to glory.\n\nBehold the man upon a cross,\nMy sins upon His shoulders;\nAshamed, I hear my mocking voice\nCall out among the scoffers.\nIt was my sin that held Him there\nUntil it was accomplished;\nHis dying breath has brought me life -\nI know that it is finished.\n\nI will not boast in anything,\nNo gifts, no power, no wisdom;\nBut I will boast in Jesus Christ,\nHis death and resurrection.\nWhy should I gain from His reward?\nI cannot give an answer;\nBut this I know with all my heart -\nHis wounds have paid my ransom.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(450,'427','I will sing of the lamb','Stuart Townend',NULL,'1997 Kingsway\'s Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(451,'428','In silent pain the eternal Son','Christopher Idle','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(452,'429','It is a thing most wonderful','William W How 1823-97',NULL,'in this version Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(453,'430','Jesus Christ,  I think upon your sacrifice','Matt Redman',NULL,'1995 Kingsway\'s Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(454,'431','Jesus in the olive grove','Fred Pratt Green','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(455,'432','King of my life, I crown you now','Jenny E Hussey 1874-1958',NULL,'1921 Hope Publishing / Copycare','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(456,'433','Man of sorrows! What a name','Philipp Bliss 1838-76',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(457,'434','My Lord, what love is this','Graham Kendrick',NULL,'1989 Make Way Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(458,'435','O perfect life of love!','Henry W Baker 1821-77','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(459,'436','No weight of gold or silver','Timothy Dudley-Smith','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(460,'437','There is a green hill far away','Cecil F Alexander 1818-95',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(461,'438','O love divine! What have you done?','Charles Wesley 1707-88','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(462,'439','O sacred head once wounded','Paulus Gerhardt 1607-76, Tr. James W. Alexander 1804-59',NULL,'in this version Praise Trust','2