','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(506,'483','Hail, O once rejected Jesus','John Bakewell 1721-1819 and others','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(507,'484','Hail to the Lord\'s anointed','James Montgomery 1771-1854',NULL,'pulic domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(508,'485','He is exalted','Twila Paris',NULL,'1985 Straightway Music/Mountain Spring/EMIChristian Music Publishing/Adm. by CopyCare','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(509,'486','Behold the glories of the Lamb','Isaac Watts 1674-1748','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(510,'487','He is Lord, he is Lord','Marvin Frey',NULL,'Copyright control','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(511,'488','Heavenly hosts in ceaseless worship','Timothy Dudley-Smith',NULL,'Author','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(512,'489','I will build my church','Graham Kendrick','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(513,'490','Jesus is King','Wendy Churchill','Jesus is King\nand I will extol him,\nGive him the glory,\nand honour his name.\nHe reigns on high,\nenthroned in the heavens,\nWord of the Father,\nexalted for us.\n\nWe have a hope\nwhich is steadfast and certain,\nGone through the curtain\nand touching the throne.\nWe have a Priest\nwho is there interceding,\nPouring his grace\non our lives day by day.\n\nWe come to him,\nour Priest and Apostle,\nClothed in his glory\nand bearing his name,\nLaying our lives\nwith gladness before him;\nFilled with his Spirit\nwe worship the King.\n\nO Holy One,\nour hearts now adore you;\nThrilled with your goodness\nwe give you our praise.\nAngels in brightness\nwith worship surround you,\nJesus, our Saviour,\nforever the same.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(514,'491','Jesus shall reign where\'er  the sun','Isaac Watts 1674-1748',NULL,'in this version praise trust','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(515,'492','Lamb of God, you now are seated','James G Deck 1802-84','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(516,'493','Look, you saints, the sight is glorious','Thomas Kelly 1769-1855',NULL,'in this version jubilate hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(517,'494','My heart is full of admiration','Graham Kendrick',NULL,'1991 Make Way Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(518,'495','Rejoice, the Lord is King','Charles Wesley 1707-88',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(519,'496','See, the conqueror mounts in triumph','Christopher Wordsworth 1807-85','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(520,'497','He walks among the golden lamps','Timothy Dudley-Smith','He walks among the golden lamps\nOn feet like burnished bronze;\nHis hair as snows of winter white,\nHis eyes with fire aflame, and bright,\nHis glorious robe of seamless light\nSurpassing Solomon','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(521,'498','The head that once was crowned with thorns','Thomas Kelly 1769-1855','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(522,'499','Worthy is the Lamb','David Hadden','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(523,'500','The Lord is King! Lift up your voice','Josiah Conder 1789-1855',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His ascension and reign'),(524,'501','Where high the heavenly temple stands','Michael Bruce 1746-67','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His priesthood and intercession'),(525,'502','Arise, my soul, arise','Charles Wesley 1707-88',NULL,'in this version Praise Trust','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His priesthood and intercession'),(526,'503','Before the throne of God above','Charitie L. Bancroft (1841-92) / Vikki Cook',NULL,'1993 PDI Worship / ADM','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His priesthood and intercession'),(527,'504','Mercy in our time of failure','','Mercy in our time of failure,\ngrace to help in time of need:\nthis sure promise of our Saviour\nis a word that we may plead.\n\nHe has passed into the heavens,\nhe is seated on the throne,\never for us interceding,\nalways caring for his own.\n\nThere is none he will not welcome,\nno request he cannot meet;\nlet us not be slow to ask him,\nlay our burdens at his feet.\n\nWe can never come too often,\nnever with a need too great,\nnever with a prayer too simple;\nonly fear to come too late.\n\nDaily on our pilgrim journey\npraise him for his matchless grace,\nlive for his immortal glory\ntill in heaven we see his face.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His priesthood and intercession'),(528,'505','With joy we contemplate  the grace','Isaac Watts 1674-1748',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His priesthood and intercession'),(529,'506','Christ is surely coming, bringing his reward','Christopher Idle',NULL,'author / Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(530,'507','Hark! The song of jubilee','James Montgomery 1771-1854','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(531,'508','I cannot tell why he whom angels worship','William Y. Fullerton 1857-1932',NULL,'Baptist Union of Great Britain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(532,'509','The King shall come, when morning dawns','tr. John Brownlie 1857-1925',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(533,'510','Jesus, Alpha and Omega','Keith Landis','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(534,'511','Lo! He comes with clouds descending','Charles Wesley',NULL,'in this version praise trust','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(535,'512','Rejoicing in hope we wait for our King','Margaret Clarkson','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(536,'513','Your Kingdom come, O God','Lewis Hensley 1824-1905',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(537,'514','When the King shall come again','Christopher Idle','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(538,'515','You are coming, O my Saviour','Frances R Havergal 1836-79',NULL,'In this version Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(539,'516','When the Lord in glory comes','Timothy Dudley-Smith','When the Lord in glory comes,\nNot the trumpets, not the drums,\nNot the anthem, not the psalm,\nNot the thunder, not the calm,\nNot the shout the heavens raise,\nNot the chorus, not the praise,\nNot the silences sublime,\nNot the sounds of space and time...\n\nBut his voice when he appears\nShall be music to my ears;\nBut his voice when he appears\nShall be music to my ears.\n\nWhen the Lord is seen again,\nNot the glories of his reign,\nNot the lightnings through the storm,\nNot the radiance of his form,\nNot his pomp and power alone,\nNot the splendours of his throne,\nNot his robe and diadems,\nNot the gold and not the gems...\n\nBut his face upon my sight\nShall be darkness into light;\nBut his face upon my sight\nShall be darkness into light.\n\nWhen the Lord to human eyes\nShall bestride our narrow skies,\nNot the child of humble birth,\nNot the carpenter of earth,\nNot the man by all denied,\nNot the victim crucified,\nBut the God who died to save,\nBut the victor of the grave...\n\nHe it is to whom I fall,\nJesus Christ, my all in all;\nHe it is to whom I fall,\nJesus Christ, my all in all.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His return in glory'),(540,'517','Breathe on me, breath of God','Edwin Hatch 1835-89',NULL,'Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Holy Spirit','His person and power'),(541,'518','Come down, O Love Divine','Bianco da Siena (1367-1434), trans. Richard F. Littledale (1833-90)',NULL,'in this version Jubilate Hymns','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Holy Spirit','His person and power'),(542,'519','Come, Holy Spirit, like a dove descending','Robert Bruce first published in New Songs and Solos, 1888','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Holy Spirit','His person and power'),(543,'520','Come, Holy Spirit, heavenly dove','Isaac Watts 1674-1748','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Holy Spirit','His person and power'),(544,'521','Into a world of dark','Ann Phillips and compilers of Rejoice and Sing','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Holy Spirit','His person and power'),(545,'522','O Holy Spirit, by whose breath','John W Grant Based on Veni Creator Spiritus John Cosin 1594','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00'