prevail,\nLeave not my trembling heart to fail.\n\nFriend of the friendless and the faint,\nWhere should I lodge my deep complaint?\nWhere, but with you, whose open door\nInvites the helpless and the poor?\n\nDid sufferers ever with you plead\nAnd you refuse them in their need?\nDoes not your promised word remain,\nThat none shall seek your face in vain?\n\nGrief such as that I could not bear,\nUnless you heard and answered prayer;\nBut a prayer-hearing, answering God\nSupports me under every load.\n\nBright is my future in your love;\nI have an advocate above:\nThose whom the world admires the most\nHave no such privilege to boast.\n\nPoor and forgotten I am, yet\nThe living God does not forget:\nAll those are safe, and must succeed\nFor whom Christ promises to plead.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Christian life','Suffering and trial'),(900,'877','How firm a foundation, you saints of the Lord','\'K\' in Rippon\'s Selection 1787',NULL,'Praise Trust','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Christian life','Suffering and trial'),(901,'878','Still near me, O my Saviour, stand','Verse 1 Charles Wesley 1707-88 Verses 2 and 3 Paulus Gerha','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Christian life','Suffering and trial'),(902,'879','Trouble may break with the dawn','Malcolm MacGregor','Trouble may break with the dawn\nAnd evil may come and darkness will fall;\nClouds will appear in the sky\nAnd tears in our eyes and pain in the soul.\nBut God stands at his people','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Christian life','Suffering and trial'),(903,'880','Christian, seek not yet repose','Charlotte Elliott 1789-1871','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Christian life','Spiritual warfare'),(904,'881','Christian, do you see them','John Mason Neale',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Christian l