 streets shine','Paul Oakley',NULL,'1995 Kingsway\'s Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00','Because of you',1,NULL,'The future','Heaven and glory'),(1131,'','This Is The Day','arranged by Roland Fudge',NULL,'1983 Roland Fudge','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1132,'','Thou Art The Everlasting Word','Josiah Conder 17889-1855','Thou art the everlasting Word,\nthe Father\'s only Son;\nGod manifestly seen and heard,\nand Heaven\'s beloved One:\n.\nWorthy, O Lamb of God, art Thou\nthat every knee to Thee should bow.\n\nIn Thee most perfectly expressed\nthe Father\'s glories shine;\nof the full Deity possesed,\neternally divine:\n.\nWorthy, O Lamb of God, art Thou\nthat every knee to Thee should bow.\n\nTrue image of the infinite,\nwhose essence is concealed;\nbrightness of uncreated light;\nthe heart of God revealed:\n.\nWorthy, O Lamb of God, art Thou\nthat every knee to Thee should bow.\n\nBut the high mysteries of Thy name\nan angel\'s grasp transcend;\nthe Father only - glorious claim!\nthe Son can comprehend:\n.\nWorthy, O Lamb of God, art Thou\nthat every knee to Thee should bow.\n\nThroughout the universe of bliss,\nthe centre Thou, and sun;\nthe eternal theme of praise is this,\nto heaven\'s beloved One:\n.\nWorthy, O Lamb of God, art Thou\nthat every knee to Thee should bow.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1133,'','To see the king of Heaven fall','','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His suffering and death'),(1134,'','We are a moment','','We are a moment, You are forever\nLord of the ages, God before time\nWe are a vapour, You are eternal\nLove everlasting, reigning on high\n\nHoly, Holy, Lord God Almighty\nWorthy is the Lamb that was slain\nHighest praises, honour and glory\nBe unto Your name, be unto Your name\n\nWe are the broken, You are the healer\nJesus, Redeemer, mighty to save\nYou are the love song, we\'ll sing forever\nBowing before You, blessing Your name\n\nHoly, Holy, Lord God Almighty\nWorthy is the Lamb that was slain\nHighest praises, honour and glory\nBe unto Your name, be unto Your name\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1135,'','We have heard a joyful sound','Priscilla Owens 1829-1907',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The gospel','Invitation and warning'),(1136,'','We Three Kings','','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1137,'','What a Whale of a Tale (Jonah\'s Song)','','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,'Children’s',NULL),(1138,'','What a Wonderful Saviour is Jesus','anon',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1139,'','What Child Is This','Neil Bennetts',NULL,'2001 Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1140,'','When I was lost','Kate & Miles Simmonds',NULL,'2001 Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'Approaching God','Adoration and thanksgiving'),(1141,'','When The Trumpet Of The Lord','James M Black 1856-1938',NULL,'Hope Publishing, adm by CopyCare','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The future','Heaven and glory'),(1142,'','Who Is This Man','','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1143,'','Who Put The Colours In The Rainbow','J.A.P. Booth',NULL,'Paul Booth/Adm. by CopyCare','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'Children’s',NULL),(1144,'','Who took fish and bread','Betty Lou Mills',NULL,'Betty Lou Mills','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1145,'','Who, O Lord, could save themselves','Matt Redman & Jonas Myrin','Who, O Lord, could save themselves,\ntheir own soul could heal?\nOur shame was deeper than the sea;\nYour grace is deeper still.\n\nAnd you alone can rescue,\nYou alone can save.\nYou alone can lift us from the grave.\nYou came down to find us,\nled us out of death.\nTo you alone belongs the highest praise.\n\nYou, O Lord, have made a way,\nthe great divide you healed;\nfor when our hearts were far away,\nyour love went further still.\nYes, your love goes further still!\n\nAnd you alone can rescue,\nYou alone can save.\nYou alone can lift us from the grave.\nYou came down to find us,\nled us out of death.\nTo you alone belongs the highest praise.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'Approaching God','Adoration and thanksgiving'),(1146,'','Why should I charge my soul with care','J H Sammis',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1147,'','Wide Wide As The Ocean','','','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1148,'','With a prayer you fed the hungry','Stuart Townend',NULL,'2002 Thankyou Music','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00','Love incarnate',0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1149,'','Worthy O Worthy Are You Lord','Mark Kinzer',NULL,'1976 The Word of God Music/Adm. by CopyCare','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The Son','His name and praise'),(1150,'','Yes, God is good','John Hampden Gurney (1802-62)',NULL,'Public Domain','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1151,'','You Are My Rock','','You are my Rock\nYou are my Mighty King\nYou are the Place where I stand\nYou are my Hope\nStrength of my life\nYou hold me safe in Your hand.\n\nWhenever I am afraid,\nI will run to You\nWhen love is far away,\nYour love breaks through.\n\nYou are my Rock\nYou are my Mighty King\nYou are the Place where I stand\nYou are my Hope\nStrength of my life\nYou hold me safe in Your hand.\n-+-','','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1152,'','You Chose The Cross','Martyn Layzell',NULL,'2002 Thankyou Music/adm','2016-10-11 08:57:00','2016-10-11 08:57:00',NULL,1,NULL,'The So